</div>
</p>

Q: How can I format a duration with std::println? A: <p><code>duration_cast</code> returns a <code>duration</code> object rather than a raw numeric value. The number shown in brackets represents the number of seconds in one year. The quick solution for your  case is to call the <code>count()</code> member function of the <code>duration</code> class. For reference: <a href="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/chrono/duration/count.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/chrono/duration/count.html</a></p>
<pre><code>duration: 1[31556952]s year(s)
</code></pre>
<pre><code>// Source - https://stackoverflow.com/q/79879480
// Posted by Angle.Bracket, modified by community. See post 'Timeline' for change history
// Retrieved 2026-01-31, License - CC BY-SA 4.0

#include &lt;print&gt;
#include &lt;chrono&gt;
#include &lt;string&gt;
int main() {
    using namespace std::chrono;
    system_clock::time_point tp1;
    system_clock::time_point tp2;

    std::string y1 = &quot;01.01.2024&quot;;
    std::string y2 = &quot;01.01.2025&quot;;

    std::istringstream is1{ y1.data() };
    is1 &gt;&gt; parse(&quot;%d.%m.%Y&quot;, tp1);
    std::istringstream is2{ y2.data() };
    is2 &gt;&gt; parse(&quot;%d.%m.%Y&quot;, tp2);

    std::println(&quot;{}&quot;, tp1); // 2024-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 
    std::println(&quot;{}&quot;, tp2); // 2025-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 

    auto duration = duration_cast&lt;years&gt;(tp2 - tp1).count(); // NOTE: Modified here
    std::println(&quot;duration: {} year(s)&quot;, duration); // duration: 1 year(s) 

    return 0;
}
</code></pre>

Q: tvOS Picker not showing checkmark for selected item A: <p>I don't have an Apple TV, but on the simulator with tvOS-26.2, the
following code adds a checkmark:</p>
<p>Example code:</p>
<pre><code>
struct ContentView: View {
    @ObservedObject var settings: MySettngs

    var body: some View {
        NavigationStack {
            Form {
                Section(&quot;Option&quot;) {
                    Picker(&quot;Option Type&quot;, selection: $settings.optionType) {
                        ForEach(OptionType.allCases) { option in
                            HStack {
                                Text(option.rawValue)
                                if option == settings.optionType {
                                    Image(systemName: &quot;checkmark&quot;)
                                }
                            }.tag(option)
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>You could also try using <code>.pickerStyle(.menu)</code> on your original Picker.</p>
<p>EDIT-1</p>
<p>If my original code does not suit you and <code>.pickerStyle(.menu)</code> does not work for you,
try this instead of the <code>Picker</code>, it gives a checkmark inside the menu, but not in the main view, and it's only a few lines of code longer:</p>
<pre><code>
                    Menu {
                        ForEach(OptionType.allCases) { option in
                            Button {
                                settings.optionType = option
                            } label: {
                                HStack {
                                    if option == settings.optionType {
                                        Image(systemName: &quot;checkmark&quot;)
                                    }
                                    Text(option.rawValue)
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    } label: {
                        HStack {
                            Text(&quot;Option Type&quot;)
                            Spacer()
                            Text(settings.optionType.rawValue)
                        }
</code></pre>
<pre><code>                }
</code></pre>

Q: How to update database in codeigniter A: <p>I haven't tested the following, but it is mostly from <a href="https://www.codeigniter.com/userguide3/libraries/form_validation.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer">the CI3 form validation documentation</a>.</p>
<p>Controller:</p>
<p>Your field populating array should have a <code>name</code> key for each form field; you mistakenly wrote the name value as the key.</p>
<p><code>$this-&gt;input-&gt;post()</code> can elegantly receive a whitelist array of submission field names.</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>public function edit_product(int $productId)
{
    $data['productId'] = $productId;

    $this-&gt;form_validation-&gt;set_rules([
        [
            'field' =&gt; 'product_name',
            'label' =&gt; 'Product name',
            'rules' =&gt; 'required'
        ],
        [
            'field' =&gt; 'username',
            'label' =&gt; 'Username',
            'rules' =&gt; 'required',
        ],
        [
            'field' =&gt; 'email',
            'label' =&gt; 'Email',
            'rules' =&gt; 'required|valid_email'
        ],
        [
            'field' =&gt; 'usertype',
            'label' =&gt; 'User type',
            'rules' =&gt; 'required'
        ]
    ]);

    if (
        $this-&gt;input-&gt;method() === 'post'
        &amp;&amp; $this-&gt;form_validation-&gt;run()
    ) {
        $submission = $this-&gt;input-&gt;post(
            ['product_name', 'username', 'email', 'usertype'], true
        );

        $data['outcome'] = $this-&gt;generalmod_model-&gt;update_product($productId, $submission))
            ? 'Updated'
            : 'No changes';
    } else {
        $data['outcome'] = null;
    }

    $product = $this-&gt;generalmod_model-&gt;get_product($productId);

    $data['product_name'] = [
        'name'  =&gt; 'product_name',
        'id'    =&gt; 'product_name',
        'type'  =&gt; 'text',
        'style' =&gt; 'width:300px;',
        'value' =&gt; set_value('product_name', $product['product_name'] ?? ''),
    ];

    $data['username'] = [
        'name'  =&gt; 'username',
        'id'    =&gt; 'username',
        'type'  =&gt; 'text',
        'style' =&gt; 'width:300px',
        'value' =&gt; set_value('username', $product['username'] ?? ''),
    ];

    $data['email'] = [
        'name'  =&gt; 'email',
        'id'    =&gt; 'email',
        'type'  =&gt; 'text',
        'style' =&gt; 'width:300px',
        'value' =&gt; set_value('email', $product['email'] ?? ''),
    ];

    $data['usertype'] = [
        'name'  =&gt; 'usertype',
        'id'    =&gt; 'usertype',
        'type'  =&gt; 'text',
        'style' =&gt; 'width:300px;',
        'value' =&gt; set_value('usertype', $product['usertype'] ?? ''),
    ];

    $this-&gt;load-&gt;view('update_profile', $data);
}
</code></pre>
<p>Model</p>
<p>The variable name being associated with the column name is a little confusing, but I trust that it is correcting your application.</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>public function get_product(int $productId): ?array
{
    return $this-&gt;db
        -&gt;select('user_id, product_name, username, email, usertype')
        -&gt;get_where('users', ['user_id' =&gt; $productId])
        -&gt;row_array();
}

public function update_product(int $productId, array $set): bool
{
    return $this-&gt;db-&gt;update('users', $set, ['user_id' =&gt; $productId])
        &amp;&amp; $this-&gt;db-&gt;affected_rows();
}
</code></pre>
<p>View:</p>
<p>Show a potential validation error message at the top of your form.</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;?php
echo $outcome ?? validation_errors();

echo form_open(&quot;generalcon/edit_product/$productId&quot;); ?&gt;
&lt;table width=&quot;700&quot; border=&quot;1&quot; cellpadding=&quot;0&quot; cellspacing=&quot;2&quot; align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;
    &lt;tr&gt;
        &lt;td width=&quot;130&quot; align=&quot;right&quot;&gt; product Name: &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;td&gt;&lt;?php echo form_input($product_name); ?&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;/tr&gt;
    &lt;tr&gt;
        &lt;td width=&quot;130&quot; align=&quot;right&quot;&gt;  username: &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;td&gt;&lt;?php echo form_input($username); ?&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;/tr&gt;
    &lt;tr&gt;
        &lt;td align=&quot;right&quot;&gt;Email:&lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;td&gt;&lt;?php echo form_input($email); ?&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;/tr&gt;
    &lt;tr&gt;
        &lt;td align=&quot;right&quot;&gt;usertype:&lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;td&gt;&lt;?php echo form_input($usertype); ?&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;/tr&gt;
    &lt;tr&gt;
        &lt;td&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;td&gt;&lt;?php echo form_submit('submit', 'Submit');?&gt;
            &lt;input type=&quot;button&quot; name=&quot;btnBack&quot; id=&quot;btnBack&quot; value=&quot;Back&quot; onclick=&quot;window.location.href='&lt;?php echo base_url() ?&gt;manage'&quot; /&gt;
        &lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
</code></pre>
